    {
      "name": "invite_membership_transition_atomicity",
      "vector_id": "ak.vector.invite.membership_transition_atomicity.v1",
      "variants": [
        "create_keeps_member_leave_then_accept_joins",
        "accept_without_pending_or_claimed_invite_prestate_is_rejected",
        "cancel_rejected_leaves_member_cell_unchanged",
        "revoke_with_expired_reason_leaves_member_cell_unchanged",
        "third_party_create_and_revoke_write_no_member_state",
        "bare_member_state_ban_from_leave_uses_membership_fsm",
        "direct_inviter_cancel_revoked_is_accepted",
        "direct_inviter_cancel_missing_or_mismatched_invitee_is_reducer_projection_failed",
        "token_invite_cancel_revoked_is_invite_kind_requires_revoke",
        "token_invite_revoke_revoked_is_accepted",
        "claimed_invite_accept_is_accepted",
        "direct_create_and_accept_release_the_live_target_slot",
        "send_failed_revoke_keeps_the_live_target_slot_claimed"
      ],
      "expected": {
        "decision": "mixed",
        "registered_write_counts": {
          "ak.invite.create": 2,
          "ak.invite.accept.directed": 3,
          "ak.invite.accept.third_party": 2,
          "ak.invite.cancel": 2,
          "ak.invite.revoke.directed_terminal": 2,
          "ak.invite.revoke.send_failed": 1,
          "ak.invite.revoke.third_party": 1
        },
        "accepted_member_state_path": [
          "leave",
          "join"
        ]
      },
      "assertions": [
        "ak.invite.create atomically writes invite.lifecycle and the invite.live_target slot while ak.invite.accept atomically writes invite.lifecycle, member.state join and the invite.live_target release",
        "the membership FSM has no invite state and exact invite acceptance uses the registered leave to join edge",
        "a rejected or revoked or expired invite changes only invite.lifecycle and leaves the member cell byte-identical",
        "the 3PID create and revoke branches produce no member.state projection; claim produces only a subject-bound membership proposal",
        "a direct member ban from leave is evaluated independently by the membership FSM",
        "ak.invite.cancel is valid only for a stored direct invitee binding; token and 3PID invites require the high-risk ak.invite.revoke path",
        "a direct cancel requires signed payload.invitee_account_id to equal the stored invitee binding",
        "claimed to accepted is a registered invite FSM edge and ak.invite.accept must derive its from state from the frozen cell",
        "a directed ak.invite.revoke to send_failed writes only invite.lifecycle and leaves the invite.live_target slot claimed",
        "a third-party ak.invite.revoke writes only invite.lifecycle because its payload carries no invitee_account_id",
        "the write count is branch-dependent, not per kind: ak.invite.accept and ak.invite.revoke derive the invite.live_target write only when the payload carries invitee_account_id, so a third-party accept is two writes and a send_failed or third-party revoke is one"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "invite_live_target_uniqueness",
      "vector_id": "ak.vector.invite.live_target_uniqueness.v1",
      "variants": [
        "second_directed_create_for_the_same_account_is_rejected_with_zero_writes",
        "concurrent_directed_creates_resolve_to_one_slot_holder",
        "terminal_release_then_reinvite_is_accepted",
        "expired_at_wall_clock_alone_does_not_release_the_slot",
        "send_failed_holder_requires_revoke_before_a_new_create",
        "third_party_revoke_forging_invitee_account_id_is_reducer_projection_failed",
        "directed_revoke_omitting_invitee_account_id_is_reducer_projection_failed",
        "release_head_eq_spelled_as_invite_id_is_failed_precondition"
      ],
      "expected": {
        "decision": "mixed",
        "occupied_error": {
          "code": "failed_precondition",
          "reason_code": "invite_live_target_occupied",
          "details_schema_ref": "schemas/service-operation-dtos.schema.json#/$defs/InviteLiveTargetOccupiedProblem"
        },
        "live_states": [
          "pending",
          "send_failed"
        ],
        "slot_value_source": "envelope.event_id"
      },
      "assertions": [
        "the only source of truth for directed invite live uniqueness is ak.component.invite.live_target.v1 whose subject is the single-component composite over canonical_json(payload.invitee_account_id) and never contains realm_id",
        "ak.invite.create carries head_eq null for that cell and the Seal additionally derives the full head-identity guard for it; a second directed create for the same account is rejected with failed_precondition and invite_live_target_occupied, enters no canonical history and derives no cell write",
        "the rejection details are closed to reason_code, invite_id and create_event_id and MUST NOT be reported as cas_conflict",
        "two concurrent directed creates contend on the same cell so exactly one wins under the CBS basis and the loser is rejected, independent of any implementation-private index or insertion order",
        "a terminal invite releases the slot with an explicit set null write that keeps its own head, and a later create for the same account is accepted; a create whose basis is pinned to an earlier free state is still rejected because the head identities differ even though both settle to null",
        "reaching expires_at does not release the slot; only a registered Move does, so the slot stays claimed until ak.invite.revoke with target_state expired is accepted",
        "send_failed keeps the slot claimed and the payload schema forbids invitee_account_id there, so the client must revoke before creating a replacement invite",
        "a third-party invite whose revoke payload carries a forged invitee_account_id fails stored_field_matches_payload with reducer_projection_failed and releases no slot",
        "a directed invite whose terminal revoke omits invitee_account_id fails the same predicate, so a directed invite cannot leak a permanently claimed slot",
        "the slot value is the literal ak:event: create_event_id; a release Move whose head_eq carries the ak:invite: spelling is failed_precondition"
      ]
    },
